@model WhenWorksWeb.Models.EventFinalizeViewModel

@* Finalize tab's "Final dates" card — split out of Finalize.cshtml so it can be rendered in
   either position (above or below "Call the date", depending on Model.CanManageEvent — see
   Finalize.cshtml) without duplicating markup.

   Its own card, not a sub-section of "Call the date", so a confirmed date reads as a bigger,
   more settled result than a suggestion, with a full h3 heading (not .ww-settings-sublabel's
   smaller sub-heading size) to match. Rows themselves are rendered client-side by the same
   WWBestBets.renderFinalDatesList the Availability tab's live "Final dates" card uses (same
   #ww-final-dates-list id, so it picks up that card's own blue-tint styling for free) — the
   per-date "N of M available" counts it shows only exist as a client-side computation over the
   calendar JSON _FinalizeCallTheDateCard loads for Suggestions, with no server-side equivalent to
   render this from directly. options.renderRemoveControl (organizer-only) adds the "x" button a
   plain Availability-tab row doesn't have.

   The empty-text paragraph and the list container both always render (rather than one or the
   other via a server @if), with whichever doesn't apply yet marked hidden, and the antiforgery
   form always renders when Model.CanManageEvent regardless of Model.FinalDates.Count — so a
   FinalDatesChanged broadcast (see Finalize.cshtml's script) that live-adds this event's first
   final date has a token ready to build a remove form against without a refresh. *@
<div class="ww-event-card mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-display mb-3">Final dates</h3>
    @* Anchored to RemoveFinalDateError (a display-only property, never bound from a form) so a
       stale RemoveFinalDate submission's error shows up here, next to the remove control the
       organizer clicked, instead of only in _FinalizeCallTheDateCard's add-date form summary. *@
    <span asp-validation-for="RemoveFinalDateError" class="text-danger d-block mb-2"></span>
    <p class="ww-people-subtitle mb-0" id="ww-final-dates-empty-text" hidden="@(Model.FinalDates.Count > 0)">No final date set yet.</p>
    <div id="ww-final-dates-list" hidden="@(Model.FinalDates.Count == 0)"></div>
    @if (Model.CanManageEvent)
    {
        <form id="ww-final-date-remove-antiforgery-form" class="visually-hidden">
            @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
        </form>
    }
</div>
